{"When refreshed response omits refresh_token, the code forces data.refresh_token = 'refresh_token' placeholder, and both Zoom/Office365 immediately write that placeholder over the credential row, so the real refresh_token is lost and all future refreshes fail; should preserve the existing token instead": 0.9468646049499512, "minimumTokenResponseSchema defines literal keys via [z.string().toString()] instead of allowing unknown keys, so the schema rejects normal refresh responses (which include expires_in, refresh_token, token_type, etc.), causing credential sync to throw 'Invalid refreshed tokens were returned'; should use .passthrough() or explicit field definitions": 0.8250539302825928, "refreshOAuthTokens now returns a raw fetch Response when credential sharing is enabled, but the handler treats the result as a gaxios response (res?.data) and reads token.access_token/expiry_date without calling res.json(), so the fields are undefined and refreshed tokens are never persisted": 0.9438908100128174, "refreshOAuthTokens call supplies credentialId, so the sync post uses calcomUserId=credentialId even though refreshOAuthTokens builds the payload from the Cal.com userId, meaning the endpoint will not load the right user's tokens; should pass credential.userId instead": 0.8981105089187622}